1 NOTE Wife of Martinus van Duijnhoven (Gen 2). The Verwegen family was a well-established Catholic family in the Uden region, with records dating back to the 18th century in the BHIC archives. Geertruda's parents were Johannes Verwegen (son of Geurt Peter Verwegen and Helena "Leen" Jan Gielens, who married 31 Jan 1773 in Boekel) and Mechelina van den Berk, who married 13 Feb 1820. The Verwegen and Van Duijnhoven families intermarried extensively: Geertruda's sister Ardina Verwegen married Martinus's brother Johannes van Duijnhoven on 26 Jan 1856, just two years before Geertruda married Martinus (17 Feb 1858) - two Verwegen sisters married two Van Duijnhoven brothers, a remarkable family arrangement common in tight-knit Catholic Brabant communities. Geertruda was mother of at least 9 children of Generation 3: Lambertus (1861), Maria (1864), Antonius (1865), Petrus Cornelus (1867), Petronella (1869), Johanna (died young ~1880), and Marianus (1872, the direct ancestor). Lived her entire life in Uden during the transformation of the sandy Brabant heathlands into productive farmland.
