1 NOTE GENERATION 2 FAMILY (1858-1903). Martinus van Duijnhoven (18 Dec 1829 - 18 Jul 1903) x Geertruda Verwegen (1833 - ~1900). Large Catholic family typical of rural Noord-Brabant during the "Rijke Roomse Leven" (Rich Roman Life) era following the 1853 restoration. Had at least 9 children: Lambertus (1861), Maria (1864), Antonius (1865), Petrus Cornelus (1867), Petronella (1869), Johanna (died young ~1870), and MARIANUS (24 Apr 1872, @I005@) — our direct ancestor. Of the male children, only Marianus survived to continue the main line; this high child mortality was tragically common. The Verwegen-Van Duijnhoven connection was a double bond: Geertruda's sister Ardina married Martinus's brother Johannes in 1856. This generation lived through the 1878-1895 European Agricultural Crisis when cheap American grain collapsed prices, forcing Dutch farmers to diversify into dairy, pigs, and sugar beets. Geertruda predeceased Martinus by ~3 years; he died 18 Jul 1903 at age 73.

