1 RELI Roman Catholic
1 NOTE Matriarch of Generation 4. Born in Boekel, a village with a unique history of Catholic religious freedom. From 1324, Boekel belonged to the Land van Ravenstein, which under Palatinate-Neuburg rule (from 1629) enjoyed religious freedom while neighboring Brabant was under Protestant States-General rule - Catholics from surrounding areas built "barn churches" on Boekel's borders to practice their faith. The Van den Elzen family was an established Boekel farming family; Anna Maria's parents were Johannes van den Elzen and Francijna van der Horst. She married Marianus 18 May 1906 in Boekel at age 27, following the tradition of marrying in the bride's parish. Mother of 12 children born 1907-1923 in Boekel and later Uden: Francina, Martinus, Gerardus, Hubertus, Jan, Johanna Maria, Johanna, Johan, Antonius, Gerarda Maria, Marinus, and Hendrica Maria. The family moved from Boekel to Uden around 1914 (Johanna was the first child born in Uden). Anna Maria was related to the wider Van den Elzen network in Boekel, which included a nun known as Zuster Cleopha who celebrated a remarkable 75-year religious jubilee. Anna Maria outlived her husband by over three years, dying 21 December 1952 at age 74, having witnessed both World Wars and the post-war recovery of the Netherlands.
