1 NOTE Parents of 12 children (Generation 4): Francina (1907), Martinus (1908), Gerardus (1909), Hubertus (1911), Jan (1912), Johanna Maria (1913), Johanna (1914, first child born after move to Uden), Johan (1915, emigrated to USA 1950), Antonius (1916), Gerarda Maria (1919), Marinus (1920), and Hendrica Maria (1923). This large Catholic family epitomized the "kinderrijk gezin" ideal of the "Rijke Roomse Leven" era in Brabant. The first seven children were born in Boekel; the family moved to Uden around 1914. Marianus and Anna Maria raised their family through WWI (Netherlands neutral but affected), the 1918 Spanish Flu pandemic, the interwar Depression, and WWII German occupation (1940-1944). Their son Johan's 1950 emigration to Minnesota continued a pattern begun when Fr. Theodore van den Broek led Uden Catholics to Wisconsin in 1848.

