1 NOTE Fourth child, third son of Marianus and Anna Maria. Named for Saint Hubertus, patron saint of hunters - a significant choice in rural Brabant where hunting supplemented farming. His birth (May 28) fell just two days before Saint Hubertus's feast day (May 30), explaining this name choice following the Catholic tradition of naming children after the saint whose feast falls nearest their birth. The Sint Hubertusviering (celebration) was especially strong in Brabant, where special blessed Hubertus rolls were baked and shared.
