1 NOTE Generation 3. Eldest daughter of Martinus van Duijnhoven (Gen 2) and Geertruda Verwegen, born 27 May 1864 in Uden. Elder sister of Marianus (1872, the direct ancestor of the American branch). Maria grew up in the "Rijke Roomse Leven" (Rich Roman Life) era of Catholic Brabant, where the Church was central to daily life - from baptism to burial, all life events were marked by religious ceremony. As the eldest daughter in a large farming family, she would have had significant responsibilities helping raise her younger siblings, a common role for firstborn daughters in this era. The Brabant tradition of naming children after grandparents and saints was strictly observed. No marriage record found; fate after 1864 birth record requires further research. Confirmed via BHIC civil registry.
1 FAMC @F014@

