1 NOTE Fairman Campbell (1912-1990) x Mary Ellen Ortscheid (1919-2012). A union bridging two distinct Midwestern Catholic communities: Fairman from Red Wing, Minnesota — a thriving Mississippi River city known for its pottery and shoe industries — and Mary Ellen from Cuba City, Wisconsin — a small town in the Upper Mississippi Valley lead-zinc mining district where mining had dominated since the 1820s. Parents of 16 children (15 reached adulthood, infant Jerome died). The size of this family — remarkable even for Catholic families of the era — reflects their deep faith and the prosperity of mid-century Red Wing. Daughters: Marion (x George Willis), Joyce (x Ted Erickson), Theresa (x Ron Stinson), Patricia (x John Smith), Mary Margaret (x Steve Reimann), Mary Cecilia (x Peter John van Duynhoven), Marie (x Dale Czapiewski), Barbara Smith (predeceased Mary Cecilia). Sons: James (x Cheryl), Wayne (x Sue), John (x Karen), Joseph (x Avis), William/Bill (x Susan Bushnell), Michael (x Cynthia), Thomas (x Ann), Steven (x Phyllis), Jerome (infant, deceased). Both parents are buried at Calvary Cemetery, Red Wing.

