2 GIVN Helena
2 SURN Gielens
2 NICK Leen Jan Gielens
1 SEX F
1 RELI Roman Catholic
1 NOTE Johannes Verwegen's mother, Geertruda Verwegen's paternal grandmother. Married Geurt Peter Verwegen on 31 January 1773 in Boekel — a village in eastern Brabant that had been part of the Catholic heerlijkheid of Ravenstein and thus enjoyed religious freedom while the surrounding Dutch Republic was officially Protestant. The designation "Jan Gielens" in her name follows the Brabant patronymic convention, indicating her father was named Jan (Johannes) Gielens. The Gielens family, like the Verwegens, were part of the farming community that worked the sandy soils of eastern Brabant. Gen -1 on Verwegen line.
1 FAMS @F027@

