1 NOTE Wilhelmus Cornelissen (b.7 Dec 1876 Bakel) x Anna Maria Verbruggen (b.14 Oct 1877 Bakel). Parents of Anna Maria Cornelissen (wife of Johan van Duijnhoven, emigrated to USA 1950). Had approximately 10 children born 1906-1922 in Bakel en Milheeze — a family size typical of Catholic farming families in this region of the Peel. Their marriage united two established Bakel families: Cornelissen (Peter Cornelissen x Johanna Verhoeven) and Verbruggen (Martinus Verbruggen x Petronella van Grootel). The village of Bakel en Milheeze, east of Helmond, was a deeply Catholic agricultural community where the 16th century St. Willibrordus Church — the oldest in the area — served as the center of religious and social life. Their daughter Anna Maria (b.30 Sep 1916) married Johan van Duijnhoven in October 1950 and emigrated to Minnesota aboard the RMS Queen Elizabeth, part of the massive Dutch post-war emigration wave that saw over 500,000 Dutch citizens leave between 1946-1972.

